AB  - In specialized domains such as public tendering and bidding, Large Language Models (LLMs) often suffer from factual ‘hallucinations’ and knowledge limitations, hindering their reliability in question-answering systems. To address this, we introduce TenderGraphRAG, a Retrieval-Augmented Generation framework built upon a high-fidelity, domain-specific knowledge graph. The cornerstone of our framework is the Human-in-the-Loop Collaborative Relation Ontology Evolution (HLC-ROE) paradigm. This novel approach synergizes LLM-driven schema discovery with expert validation in a closed loop, enabling the rapid and accurate construction of the domain knowledge graph. At query time, TenderGraphRAG employs a hybrid retrieval strategy, fusing structured graph path traversal, sparse keyword (BM25) search, and dense vector search. Experimental results on our self-constructed tendering and bidding QA dataset show that TenderGraphRAG substantially outperforms a spectrum of baselines, from traditional keyword-based (BM25-RAG) and standard vector-based (NaiveRAG) systems to advanced graph-enhanced frameworks. Notably, compared to the graph-enhanced LightRAG system, our framework achieves an 11.4 percent higher accuracy (0.824 vs. 0.740) and a 17.0 percent higher completeness score (0.908 vs. 0.776). These results demonstrate that deep domain specialization, anchored by a high-fidelity knowledge graph, is a highly effective strategy for enhancing the reasoning and factual grounding of RAG systems in complex professional fields.
