AB  - Understanding and characterizing populations at a global scale is critical to many tasks such as humanitarian response, disease modeling, among others. Recent advances in Artificial Intelligence (AI) have enabled the use of large language models (LLMs) to provide advanced capabilities to assist in data acquisition tasks as the volume of data has been increasing. However, LLMs can become outdated due to the date at which the model was trained. To address this, attention has turned to the development of Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG) systems to improve upon traditional LLM chatbots for domain-specific tasks. While there are various domains in which LLMs and RAGs have revolutionized, geospatial data acquisition, particularly for population information, has remained under-studied. Here, we showcase a workflow which 1) develops a RAG framework from one consistent population corpus and 2) integrates administrative boundaries for a heightened awareness of population information and spatial cognition. We display up to 34% improvement when compared with LLMs such as Mixtral 7x8B, Gemini flash 2.5, and ChatGPT-5, highlighting the ability for our approach to generate accurate and cohesive population results. Furthermore, LLMs such as ChatGPT-5 returned multiple different population sources on successive days for the same query while our approach ensures consistent, authoritative responses critical for humanitarian decision-making. Our findings show that it is possible to leverage one consistent source of population information with geospatial data in a user-friendly interface, which can assist humanitarian responses during conflicts and extreme events.
