AB  - In today's digital world almost every online applications in various sectors such as banking, telecommunications, E-commerce etc., are facilitating customers through chatbots to improve customer experience. But, the currently existing chatbots are mostly either textual or audio based and are limited to predefined set of queries and is mostly in english language. Thus it is limiting the user experience and restricting the vernacular language speakers. As per the EF English Proficiency Index (EF EPI) 2024-25, statistics suggest that just roughly 10.6% of the Indian population speaks English language. Hence the current chatbots limit itself in the reachability to vernacular language speakers. In this paper we are demonstrating a multilingual humanoid chatbot for educational institution that facilitate human-like support experience that is capable of communicating in multiple languages. The chatbot can communicate in multiple local languages via audio conversations, expanding its reachability to vernacular speakers. The use of Artificial Intelligence will unlock the diversity of the queries unlike traditional chatbots which restricts the user to a set of predefined queries. To provide a visual representation of the engagement between the user and the chatbot, a 3D humanoid character is integrated and animated in real-time to simulate a true-to-life conversation experience between the user and the avatar. Hence, the online applications will reach to vernacular and rural population.
