AB  - In today's digital world, people are utilizing digital platforms to find solutions to their day-to-day problems. With the recent advancements in large language models (LLMs) and artificial intelligence in general, more and more multiservice solutions are emerging to provide safety and comfort, as well as to solve life's challenges. In this paper, we use the power of LLM and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to provide spiritual guidance to individuals in response to their queries, as if they were receiving it from a spiritual master or a faithful disciple of a spiritual master. Such a chatbot needs to have the capability to understand the nuances, including the context and cultural intricacies embedded in the query. Our implementation leverages the DeepSeek model, fine-tuned using LoRA on a curated dataset of spiritual texts and question-answer pairs. Fine-tuning ensures that the chatbot produces responses that are meaningful and tailored to the user's needs. Initial experimental results indicate that our approach is effective in producing semantically richer and more aligned responses with training data, demonstrating the potential of domain-adapted RAG architectures in spiritual guidance applications.
