AB  - The mining industry in India has developed Acts, Rules, Regulations, Directorate General of Mines Safety (DGMS) Circulars, and Court of Inquiry (CoI) cases. When it comes to stakeholders, they make mistakes and take a lot of time in viewing and comprehending these records. To solve this problem, an AI-powered chatbot with Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) has been created. This provides fast, instant and straightforward responses to questions on mining queries. The system is a combination of a vector-based legal knowledge base with a Large Language Model to provide factual consistency and permit. The chatbot contains information about key mining legislations such as the Coal Mines Act of 1952, the Indian Explosives Act, 1884, and land acquisition provisions. The provided work suggests that AI-based solutions can enhance the accessibility of regulations, make mining safer and accelerate the mining industry to be digitalized.
