AB  - An artificial intelligence-based drug discovery platform has been developed to leverage the therapeutic potential of Indian medicinal plants using a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) architecture. This system integrates structured knowledge bases, including taxonomic and phytochemical datasets, with traditional Ayurvedic literature and contemporary biomedical research to enable semantic search, knowledge graph construction, and drug candidate prediction. Core functionalities include a semantic search engine, a comprehensive medicinal plant knowledge graph, a RAG-based question-answering module, and an interactive research dashboard. By employing vector databases (e.g., FAISS, Pinecone), graph databases (Neo4j), and advanced language models such as BioBERT and Mistral, the platform effectively bridges the gap between ancient herbal wisdom and modern pharmacological methods. Initial performance metrics of single agent RAG show a RAG BERTScore F1 of 0.789 and an LLM BERTScore F1 of 0.779 for therapeutic use queries, demonstrating robust capabilities in information retrieval and contextual generation. This approach offers a culturally grounded, scalable solution to accelerate drug discovery and innovation in global healthcare.
