AB  - As complex industrial micorgrids, modern ports increasingly depend on AI-assisted maintenance for the monitoring and assessment of their critical assets. However, the effectiveness of these AI systems is hindered by significant big data analytics challenges, while traditional operational models struggle with knowledge transfer and process standardization from vast, unstructured data sources. These impede the provision of effective Operations and Maintenance services. To address these issues and enhance intelligent question-answering capabilities, this paper proposes a Domain Knowledge Graph assisted Retrieval Augmented Generation (DomainKG-RAG) framework, targeting the main crance devices in port microgirds. Key features include: 1) integration of a knowledge graph (KG) into the RAG process; 2) utilization of a Large Language Model (LLM) optimized via Prompt Tuning for the automated construction of the knowledge graph for answer generation; 3) construction of a domain-specific evaluation dataset and benchmarks to address the scarcity of RAG evaluation data for port machinery devices maintenance. This paper details the architecture, implementation, and performance validation of the proposed approach. Experimental results demonstrate that DomainKG-RAG outperforms baseline models across core metrics such as comprehensiveness, diversity, faithfulness, and contextual relevance, which validates its effectiveness for applications in specialized domains.
