AB  - With the advent of a changing employment scenario and growing demand for customized advice, traditional systems of career guidance are inadequate considering their contextual awareness limitation and fixed advice generation. In this paper, we present a new AI-driven chatbot with a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) model to provide intelligent, contextual, and adaptive career recommendations customized to individual users. The goal is to improve career guidance quality and availability by combining natural language generation, semantic search, and predictive analytics into one system that can scale. Three main components constitute the chatbot: a semantic search layer upon Sentence Transformers (all-mpnet-base-v2) to map the queries to vectors and output similar documents against an in-memory vector database of high-quality content; a StableLM-Zephyr-3B(LLM) model to generate crisp and natural-language responses; and a Random Forest Regression model that forecasts salary ranges based on user inputs such as occupation, industry, education level, experience, and location. Experimental evaluation verifies that the system described is better than traditional retrieval-only and generation-only methods in response appropriateness, factuality, and system performance. The salary prediction model effectively mimics real labor market trends, and quantized model usage enables high-speed, low-resource operation without compromising output quality. This RAG-based approach offers a solid foundation for scalable, AI-enabled career guidance systems. It fills the gap between passive provision of information and adaptive career consciousness, and has potential applications in educational guidance, labor market analysis, and workforce planning.
