AB  - This study presents the development of a customer service chatbot. A dataset collected from a restaurant covers various aspects, including menu and dish consultation, service incidents, practical usage scenarios, operational information, and general customer inquiries. Using this dataset, the LLaMA 3.2-1B-Instruct model was fine-tuned on domain-specific conversation pairs to tailor the language model to the target application. To improve accuracy and flexibility, the system integrates Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) with Qdrant vector search and BM25 keyword search in a hybrid retrieval framework. We evaluated the performance using automated metrics (ROUGE, BERT-Score) on the baseline and fine-tuned models, and LLM-based evaluation (RAGAS) on the RAG system. Evaluations were conducted on both the original and quantized versions (8-bit and 4-bit). The experimental results demonstrate that the proposed RAG-based chatbot system generates natural and contextually appropriate responses, and further confirm the feasibility of using quantized versions for deployment on resourceconstrained hardware.
