AB  - Student mental health challenges, such as stress, anxiety, and social isolation, often go unaddressed due to stigma and limited access to support services. To provide timely support, this work presents an Agentic AI-Based Multimodal Emotion-Aware Mental Health Chatbot that combines text and facial emotion recognition for comprehensive affect detection. The system employs a finetuned DistilBERT model for text-based emotion classification and AWS Rekognition for real-time facial emotion analysis through a custom Facial Emotion Recognition (FER) interface. An n8n workflow enables agentic automation, coordinating multimodal fusion, severity classification, and LLM-driven responses. Specialized LLM agents use Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to generate context-aware, empathetic outputs aligned with user states, while high-severity cases are escalated via Slack for human review. All detected emotions are stored in Supabase to maintain structured system records. Experimental results show that multimodal fusion improves accuracy to 94\%, outperforming text-only (92\%) and facial-only (88.3\%), with 2.3-second latency, demonstrating the system’s real-time effectiveness.
