AB  - In contemporary digitized society, individuals typically store personal documents in the digital media, like Aadhaar cards, PAN cards, hall tickets, and certificates. This manual process is inefficient and time-consuming to search particular information on these files manually. The proposed system aims to solve this challenge by combining secure web technologies with the power of multimodal Artificial Intelligence. Accessing and handling personal information on fragmented digital platforms can be very difficult for the end user, necessitating the accurate maintenance of storage sites and search syntaxes. The current paper provides a web- based chatbot based on AI, which transforms access to personal data by using natural language interfaces. The system also uses a Large Language Model (LLM) to interpret user queries, automatically determining the fields of requested data and retrieving the required information automatically through a structured database. The chatbot allows easy access to informative data, preserving privacy by adopting a secure architecture along with strict validation protocols. The system was able to read various query phrases, and it was able to retrieve personal information with accuracy of 96.5% such as ages of birth, identification numbers and contact details. Such a strategy shows tremendous possibilities of improving personal information management by using conversational AI.
