AB  - Multilingual Legal Question Answering (Legal QA) has attracted increasing attention with the rapid development of large language models (LLMs). However, reliable Legal QA depends largely on effective semantic retrieval, particularly for morphologically rich Turkic languages such as Kazakh, Uzbek, and Turkish. Existing Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) systems rely on static retrieval pipelines that insufficiently address language-specific lexical and legal terminology variations. This paper proposes an Adaptive Semantic Retrieval Framework integrating language-aware query normalization, terminology expansion, adaptive retrieval, document re-ranking, and LLM-based legal reasoning. The framework was evaluated on multilingual legal corpora comprising 6,586 legal documents, 357,568 sentences, and 3,467 manually verified question-answer pairs. Experimental results show consistent improvements over conventional retrieval methods, achieving Precision@5 values of 0.891, 0.873, and 0.918 for Kazakh, Uzbek, and Turkish, respectively, while increasing ROUGE-L from 0.731 to 0.781 and the expert score from 4.57 to 4.83. These results demonstrate that adaptive semantic retrieval substantially improves multilingual Legal QA and provides a scalable framework for Legal AI in Turkic languages
