AB  - This article introduces Electronic Device Question-Answering (ElecDevQA), a high-quality, ground-truth question-answering (QA) dataset specifically for the electronic device domain. The dataset curation commenced with the creation of a specialized knowledge graph (KG) based on data sourced from IEEE and MDPI abstracts. The procedure entailed recognizing electronic device entities and their six key information types: 1) function; 2) feature; 3) technique; 4) material; 5) composition; and 6) property. By leveraging the structured nature of the KG, we formulated six distinct types of questions. For each question, we employed a hybrid retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) approach, combining insights from our KG with relevant information from documents and web pages found via Google Search to produce accurate answers. To validate the dataset’s integrity and significance, we assessed the efficacy of ten large language models (LLMs) on this QA task. We compared their unreferenced answers to our hybrid-RAG generated answers using four distinct evaluation methods. The dataset provides a crucial benchmark for the electronic device domain and illustrates the benefits of a knowledge-based RAG approach for improving the factual accuracy and completeness of LLM responses. IEEE SOCIETY/COUNCIL Computer Society (CS) DATA TYPE/LOCATION Text (.json); Padova, Italy DATA DOI/PID 10.21227/rfj1-2z12
